<title>SWEDEN: Danish agent says Asiana air cargo 200 tonnes June.</title>
<headline>Danish agent says Asiana air cargo 200 tonnes June.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's Weco Air Cargo, general cargo sales agent for South Korean air carrier Asiana Airlines, said on Thursday it trucked about 200 tonnes of cargo from the Nordic region in June.</p>
<p>The private airline launched non-stop flights from Germany, Belgium and Austria at the end of May. It appointed Weco Air Cargo, part of the Danish privately-owned Weco Transport group, as its general sales agent as of June 1.</p>
<p>&quot;We have regularly scheduled trucks to Amsterdam, Frankfurt and Brussels from all over the Nordic region. We had close to 200 tonnes in June,&quot; Torben Olsen, director cargo at Weco Air Cargo, told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;We are feeding mainly to the Amsterdam flights from Scandinavia, but also to Frankfurt and Brussels,&quot; Olsen added.</p>
<p>-- Abigail Schmelz, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1003</p>
</text>
